IMPORT prelude

-- Constitution of the Republic of Singapore -- the fundamental liberties a person meets on arrest, at trial, at school and in
-- dealing with the State (Arts 9, 11, 12, 16), who may stand for Parliament (Arts 44, 45), and how citizenship is acquired, kept,
-- renounced and lost (Arts 121, 122, 123, 126, 128, 129).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/CONS1963.txt. The deposit
-- describes itself as the "version in force from 15/9/2026"; the latest amendment annotated is Act 9 of 2025 (in force
-- 15/09/2026; the passages it annotates concern the Maintenance of Racial Harmony Act 2025). The revised edition itself
-- incorporates amendments up to 1 December 2021.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Chosen for its everyday-life relevance to ordinary people in Singapore: it fixes what happens on arrest, bars
-- some kinds of discrimination, decides who is a citizen, and who may be a Member of Parliament. SCOPED to those provisions.
-- Not encoded: Part 3 sovereignty and referendums, Part 5 (the President, including the elected-President
-- qualifications, and the Executive), Part 5A (Council of Presidential Advisers), the Legislature beyond Arts 44-45 (vacation of seats under Art 46 included),
-- the Judiciary, the Public Service, finance, Art 13 movement, Arts 10, 14 and 15 (forced labour; speech, assembly and
-- association; religion), citizenship by naturalisation (Art 127), deprivation under Arts 129(2), (4)-(6), 130, 134, 135, the procedure in
-- Art 133, Part 12 special powers against subversion and emergency, and the Schedules.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Constitution of the Republic of Singapore -- rights and citizenship`

§§ `Article 9 -- arrest`

-- Art 9(3): "Where a person is arrested, he shall be informed as soon as may be of the grounds of his arrest and shall be allowed
-- to consult and be defended by a legal practitioner of his choice."
-- Art 9(4): an arrested person not released shall, "without unreasonable delay, and in any case within 48 hours (excluding the
-- time of any necessary journey), be produced before a Magistrate ... and shall not be further detained in custody without the
-- Magistrate's authority".
-- Art 9(5): clauses (3) and (4) do not apply "to an enemy alien or to any person arrested for contempt of Parliament pursuant to
-- a warrant issued under the hand of the Speaker".
-- Art 9(6) saves pre-Constitution public-safety detention laws and drug-rehabilitation detention laws from clauses (3) and (4);
-- that saving is not encoded. Only the 48-hour ceiling is modelled: a shorter delay may still be "unreasonable".
GIVEN `is an enemy alien` IS A BOOLEAN, `arrested for contempt of Parliament on the Speaker's warrant` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `clauses 9(3) and 9(4) protect the arrested person` IF
    (NOT `is an enemy alien`) AND (NOT `arrested for contempt of Parliament on the Speaker's warrant`)

GIVEN `hours held excluding necessary journeys` IS A NUMBER, `was released` IS A BOOLEAN, `was produced before a Magistrate` IS A BOOLEAN, `protected by 9(4)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the detention exceeds the 48-hour ceiling` IF
        `protected by 9(4)`
    AND (NOT `was released`)
    AND (NOT `was produced before a Magistrate`)
    AND `hours held excluding necessary journeys` GREATER THAN 48

§§ `Article 11 -- retrospective punishment and repeated trials`

-- Art 11(1): "No person shall be punished for an act or omission which was not punishable by law when it was done or made, and no
-- person shall suffer greater punishment for an offence than was prescribed by law at the time it was committed."
-- Art 11(2): a person convicted or acquitted "shall not be tried again for the same offence except where the conviction or
-- acquittal has been quashed and a retrial ordered by a court superior to that by which he was convicted or acquitted".
GIVEN `punishable when done` IS A BOOLEAN, `maximum prescribed when committed` IS A NUMBER, `punishment imposed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the punishment offends Article 11(1)` IF
    (NOT `punishable when done`) OR `punishment imposed` GREATER THAN `maximum prescribed when committed`

GIVEN `previously convicted or acquitted` IS A BOOLEAN, `same offence` IS A BOOLEAN, `quashed with a retrial ordered by a superior court` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a second trial is barred` IF
    `previously convicted or acquitted` AND `same offence` AND (NOT `quashed with a retrial ordered by a superior court`)

§§ `Articles 12 and 16 -- equal protection and education`

-- Art 12(1): "All persons are equal before the law and entitled to the equal protection of the law."
-- Art 12(2): "Except as expressly authorised by this Constitution, there shall be no discrimination against citizens of Singapore
-- on the ground only of religion, race, descent or place of birth" in any law, public appointment or employment, or the
-- administration of laws on property or on carrying on a trade, business, profession, vocation or employment.
-- Art 12(3): does not invalidate (a) "any provision regulating personal law"; or (b) restricting office or employment connected
-- with a religion, or a religious institution, to persons professing that religion.
-- Art 16(1): the same four grounds, for admission and fees at publicly maintained educational institutions and public financial
-- aid to students. Sex, age and other grounds are not among the four named grounds in either Article.
DECLARE Ground IS ONE OF
    religion
    race
    descent
    `place of birth`
    sex
    age
    `political opinion`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground is named in Articles 12(2) and 16(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN religion THEN TRUE
    WHEN race THEN TRUE
    WHEN descent THEN TRUE
    WHEN `place of birth` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A Ground, `against a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `on that ground only` IS A BOOLEAN, `expressly authorised by the Constitution` IS A BOOLEAN, `personal law or religious office` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the discrimination is barred by Article 12(2)` IF
        `the ground is named in Articles 12(2) and 16(1)` `the ground`
    AND `against a citizen`
    AND `on that ground only`
    AND (NOT `expressly authorised by the Constitution`)
    AND (NOT `personal law or religious office`)

-- Art 16(3): "No person shall be required to receive instruction in or to take part in any ceremony or act of worship of a
-- religion other than his own." Art 16(4): "the religion of a person under the age of 18 years shall be decided by his parent or
-- guardian."
GIVEN `age of the pupil` IS A NUMBER, `instruction is in the religion the pupil professes` IS A BOOLEAN, `instruction is in the religion the parent or guardian decided` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the pupil may be required to receive the instruction` IF
    IF `age of the pupil` LESS THAN 18
    THEN `instruction is in the religion the parent or guardian decided`
    ELSE `instruction is in the religion the pupil professes`

§§ `Articles 44 and 45 -- who may be a Member of Parliament`

-- Art 44(2): qualified if (a) a citizen; (b) "of the age of 21 years or above on the day of nomination"; (c) on a current register
-- of electors; (d) resident at nomination "and has been so resident for periods amounting in the aggregate to not less than 10
-- years prior to that date"; (e) able to speak and (unless incapacitated) read and write English, Malay, Mandarin or Tamil well
-- enough to take an active part in proceedings; (f) not disqualified under Art 45.
-- Art 45(1): disqualified if (a) found or declared of unsound mind; (b) an undischarged bankrupt; (c) holds an office of profit;
-- (d) failed to lodge a return of election expenses; (e) convicted "and sentenced to imprisonment for a term of not less than one
-- year or to a fine of not less than $10,000", without a free pardon -- a foreign conviction counts only for an offence that would
-- be punishable in Singapore; (f) "has voluntarily acquired the citizenship of, or exercised rights of citizenship in, a foreign
-- country or has made a declaration of allegiance to a foreign country"; (g) disqualified under election-offences law.
-- Art 45(2): (d) and (e) may be removed by the President and otherwise "cease at the end of 5 years beginning from" the date the
-- return was due, the release from custody, or the imposition of the fine; and no (f) disqualification "by reason only of anything
-- done by him before he became a citizen".
DECLARE Candidate HAS
    `is a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `age on nomination day` IS A NUMBER
    `is on a current register of electors` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is resident at nomination` IS A BOOLEAN
    `aggregate years resident` IS A NUMBER
    `has the language proficiency` IS A BOOLEAN
    `found to be of unsound mind` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is an undischarged bankrupt` IS A BOOLEAN
    `holds an office of profit` IS A BOOLEAN
    `failed to lodge an election expenses return` IS A BOOLEAN
    `months of imprisonment imposed` IS A NUMBER
    `fine imposed` IS A NUMBER
    `received a free pardon` IS A BOOLEAN
    `convicted by a foreign court` IS A BOOLEAN
    `offence punishable in Singapore` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years since the return was due or release or fine` IS A NUMBER
    `removed by the President` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took foreign citizenship, rights or allegiance` IS A BOOLEAN
    `did so only before becoming a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN
    `disqualified under election-offences law` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the conviction disqualifies` IF
        (    `the candidate`'s `months of imprisonment imposed` AT LEAST 12
         OR  `the candidate`'s `fine imposed` AT LEAST 10000)
    AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `received a free pardon`)
    AND (    (NOT `the candidate`'s `convicted by a foreign court`)
         OR  `the candidate`'s `offence punishable in Singapore`)

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is disqualified under Article 45` IF
        `the candidate`'s `found to be of unsound mind`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `is an undischarged bankrupt`
    OR  `the candidate`'s `holds an office of profit`
    OR  (    (`the candidate`'s `failed to lodge an election expenses return` OR `the conviction disqualifies` `the candidate`)
         AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `removed by the President`)
         AND `the candidate`'s `years since the return was due or release or fine` LESS THAN 5)
    OR  (`the candidate`'s `took foreign citizenship, rights or allegiance` AND (NOT `the candidate`'s `did so only before becoming a citizen`))
    OR  `the candidate`'s `disqualified under election-offences law`

GIVEN `the candidate` IS A Candidate
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the candidate is qualified to be a Member of Parliament` IF
        `the candidate`'s `is a citizen`
    AND `the candidate`'s `age on nomination day` AT LEAST 21
    AND `the candidate`'s `is on a current register of electors`
    AND `the candidate`'s `is resident at nomination`
    AND `the candidate`'s `aggregate years resident` AT LEAST 10
    AND `the candidate`'s `has the language proficiency`
    AND (NOT `the candidate is disqualified under Article 45` `the candidate`)

§§ `Article 121 -- citizenship by birth`

-- Art 121(1): "every person born in Singapore after 16 September 1963 shall be a citizen of Singapore by birth", but (2) not if at
-- birth (a) his father, not a citizen, had an envoy's immunity; (b) his father was an enemy alien and the birth was in a place under
-- enemy occupation; or (c) "neither of his parents was a citizen of Singapore". (3): the Government "may, where it considers it
-- just and fair", confer citizenship on a person born in Singapore notwithstanding (2)(c) -- a discretion, not encoded.
GIVEN `born in Singapore after 16 September 1963` IS A BOOLEAN, `a parent was a citizen at the birth` IS A BOOLEAN, `father was a non-citizen envoy with immunity` IS A BOOLEAN, `father was an enemy alien in an occupied place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person is a citizen by birth` IF
        `born in Singapore after 16 September 1963`
    AND `a parent was a citizen at the birth`
    AND (NOT `father was a non-citizen envoy with immunity`)
    AND (NOT `father was an enemy alien in an occupied place`)

§§ `Article 122 -- citizenship by descent`

-- Art 122(1): born outside Singapore after 16 September 1963 is a citizen by descent if at birth (a) [born before commencement of
-- s 7 of the Constitution of the Republic of Singapore (Amendment) Act 2004] "his father is a citizen of Singapore, by birth or
-- registration"; (b) [born on or after it] "either his father or mother is a citizen of Singapore, by birth, registration or
-- descent". The deposit does not give that commencement date; it is a flag here.
-- Art 122(2): only if (a) the birth is registered "within one year, or such longer period as the Government permits"; and (b) he
-- would not acquire the birth country's citizenship by birth there, where [before 2004] the father, or [after] "either his father or
-- mother", is a citizen by registration.
-- Art 122(3): a child of a parent who is a citizen by descent is not a citizen by descent unless that parent has lawfully resided in
-- Singapore (a) "not less than 5 years before that person's birth" in aggregate; or (b) "not less than 2 years during the period of
-- 5 years immediately preceding" the birth.
-- Read literally, (2)(b) and (3) bite whenever EITHER parent has the status named, even where the other parent alone would qualify
-- the child. Citizenship by naturalisation is not among the parental statuses in (1).
DECLARE Status IS ONE OF
    `not a citizen`
    `citizen by birth`
    `citizen by registration`
    `citizen by descent`
    `citizen by naturalisation`

DECLARE BirthAbroad HAS
    `father` IS A Status
    `mother` IS A Status
    `born on or after the 2004 amendment` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered in time` IS A BOOLEAN
    `acquires the birth country's citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN
    `descent parent's aggregate years of lawful residence` IS A NUMBER
    `descent parent's years of lawful residence in the last 5 years` IS A NUMBER

GIVEN `s` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is birth or registration` IF
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `citizen by birth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `citizen by registration` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `s` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is birth, registration or descent` IF
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `citizen by birth` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `citizen by registration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `citizen by descent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `s` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is registration` IF
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `citizen by registration` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `s` IS A Status
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is descent` IF
    CONSIDER `s`
    WHEN `citizen by descent` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `b` IS A BirthAbroad
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a parent qualifies under 122(1)` IF
    IF `b`'s `born on or after the 2004 amendment`
    THEN `is birth, registration or descent` (`b`'s `father`) OR `is birth, registration or descent` (`b`'s `mother`)
    ELSE `is birth or registration` (`b`'s `father`)

GIVEN `b` IS A BirthAbroad
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 122(2)(b) condition applies` IF
    IF `b`'s `born on or after the 2004 amendment`
    THEN `is registration` (`b`'s `father`) OR `is registration` (`b`'s `mother`)
    ELSE `is registration` (`b`'s `father`)

GIVEN `b` IS A BirthAbroad
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the 122(3) residence condition is met` IF
        (    (NOT `is descent` (`b`'s `father`))
         AND (NOT `is descent` (`b`'s `mother`)))
    OR  `b`'s `descent parent's aggregate years of lawful residence` AT LEAST 5
    OR  `b`'s `descent parent's years of lawful residence in the last 5 years` AT LEAST 2

GIVEN `b` IS A BirthAbroad
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the child is a citizen by descent` IF
        `a parent qualifies under 122(1)` `b`
    AND `b`'s `registered in time`
    AND (    (NOT `the 122(2)(b) condition applies` `b`)
         OR  (NOT `b`'s `acquires the birth country's citizenship`))
    AND `the 122(3) residence condition is met` `b`

-- Art 122(4): a person who as a minor becomes a citizen by descent "shall cease to be a citizen of Singapore on attaining the age of
-- 22 years unless within 12 months after he attains the age of 21 years he takes the Oath of Renunciation, Allegiance and Loyalty"
-- (and, where the Government requires, divests foreign citizenship -- not encoded). Art 126(3) says the same of a minor registered
-- under Art 124.
GIVEN `current age` IS A NUMBER, `took the oath between 21 and 22` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the minor-acquired citizenship continues` IF
    `current age` LESS THAN 22 OR `took the oath between 21 and 22`

§§ `Articles 123 and 126 -- citizenship by registration`

-- Art 123(1): a person resident in Singapore "of or over the age of 21 years" may be registered if he satisfies the Government that
-- he (a) is of good character; (b) "has resided in Singapore throughout the 12 months immediately preceding" the application; (c)
-- has resided at least 10 years in aggregate in the preceding 12 -- the Government may exempt where (i) he has 5 years in the
-- preceding 6, or (ii) "in any special case"; (d) intends to reside permanently; (e) has an elementary knowledge of Malay, English,
-- Mandarin or Tamil -- the Government "may exempt an applicant who has attained the age of 45 years or who is deaf or dumb".
-- Art 126(1): no registration under Art 123 "until he has taken the Oath of Renunciation, Allegiance and Loyalty". (2): a person who
-- renounced or was deprived of citizenship may be registered only "with the approval of the Government".
-- Registration remains a discretion ("may"); this encodes only whether the Constitution lets it happen.
DECLARE Applicant HAS
    `applicant's age` IS A NUMBER
    `is resident` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is of good character` IS A BOOLEAN
    `resided throughout the last 12 months` IS A BOOLEAN
    `years resided in the last 12` IS A NUMBER
    `years resided in the last 6` IS A NUMBER
    `residence exemption granted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is a special case` IS A BOOLEAN
    `intends to reside permanently` IS A BOOLEAN
    `has elementary language knowledge` IS A BOOLEAN
    `language exemption granted` IS A BOOLEAN
    `is deaf or dumb` IS A BOOLEAN
    `took the oath` IS A BOOLEAN
    `previously renounced or deprived` IS A BOOLEAN
    `Government approves re-registration` IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN `a` IS AN Applicant
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may be registered under Article 123(1)` IF
        `a`'s `applicant's age` AT LEAST 21
    AND `a`'s `is resident`
    AND `a`'s `is of good character`
    AND `a`'s `resided throughout the last 12 months`
    AND (    `a`'s `years resided in the last 12` AT LEAST 10
         OR  (    `a`'s `residence exemption granted`
              AND (`a`'s `years resided in the last 6` AT LEAST 5 OR `a`'s `is a special case`)))
    AND `a`'s `intends to reside permanently`
    AND (    `a`'s `has elementary language knowledge`
         OR  (    `a`'s `language exemption granted`
              AND (`a`'s `applicant's age` AT LEAST 45 OR `a`'s `is deaf or dumb`)))
    AND `a`'s `took the oath`
    AND ((NOT `a`'s `previously renounced or deprived`) OR `a`'s `Government approves re-registration`)

-- Art 123(2): "any woman who is married to a citizen of Singapore" may be registered if she satisfies the Government that she has
-- "resided continuously in Singapore for a period of not less than 2 years immediately preceding" the application, intends to reside
-- permanently, and is of good character. The clause names only a woman; no matching clause for a husband was found in Part 10.
-- The oath (Art 126(1)) and re-registration bar (Art 126(2)) apply, as for clause (1).
GIVEN `is a woman` IS A BOOLEAN, `married to a citizen` IS A BOOLEAN, `years of continuous residence` IS A NUMBER, `intends to stay permanently` IS A BOOLEAN, `of good character` IS A BOOLEAN, `has taken the oath` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the spouse may be registered under Article 123(2)` IF
        `is a woman`
    AND `married to a citizen`
    AND `years of continuous residence` AT LEAST 2
    AND `intends to stay permanently`
    AND `of good character`
    AND `has taken the oath`

§§ `Article 128 -- renunciation`

-- Art 128(1): a citizen "of or over the age of 21 years and of sound mind who is also or is about to become a citizen of another
-- country may renounce" by declaration registered by the Government. (3): applies to "a woman under the age of 21 years who has been
-- married" as if of age.
-- Art 128(2): the Government may withhold registration (a) during any war in which Singapore is engaged; or (b) for a person subject
-- to the Enlistment Act 1970 unless he has (i) discharged his liability for full-time service; (ii) "rendered at least 3 years of
-- operationally ready national service" in lieu; or (iii) complied with conditions the Government determines.
GIVEN `age now` IS A NUMBER, `is a married woman` IS A BOOLEAN, `of sound mind` IS A BOOLEAN, `has or is about to have another citizenship` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the citizen may renounce` IF
        (`age now` AT LEAST 21 OR `is a married woman`)
    AND `of sound mind`
    AND `has or is about to have another citizenship`

GIVEN `during a war` IS A BOOLEAN, `subject to the Enlistment Act` IS A BOOLEAN, `discharged full-time service` IS A BOOLEAN, `years of operationally ready service in lieu` IS A NUMBER, `met Government conditions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may withhold registration of the renunciation` IF
        `during a war`
    OR  (    `subject to the Enlistment Act`
         AND (NOT `discharged full-time service`)
         AND `years of operationally ready service in lieu` LESS THAN 3
         AND (NOT `met Government conditions`))

§§ `Article 129(3)(b)(i) and (7) -- deprivation after a sentence`

-- Art 129(3)(b)(i): the Government may deprive "any citizen of Singapore by registration or by naturalisation" if satisfied that
-- "within the period of 5 years after registration or naturalisation" he has "been sentenced in any country to imprisonment for a
-- term of not less than one year or to a fine of not less than $5,000", without a free pardon.
-- Art 129(7): no deprivation "unless the Government is satisfied that it is not conducive to the public good" that he remain a
-- citizen, and none under (3)(b)(i) "if the Government is satisfied that as a result of the deprivation he would not be a citizen
-- of any country". A citizen by birth or descent is outside Art 129 altogether.
GIVEN `the status` IS A Status, `years after registration or naturalisation` IS A NUMBER, `months of imprisonment` IS A NUMBER, `fine` IS A NUMBER, `pardoned` IS A BOOLEAN, `continuing is not conducive to the public good` IS A BOOLEAN, `would be stateless` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Government may deprive for the sentence` IF
        CONSIDER `the status`
        WHEN `citizen by registration` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `citizen by naturalisation` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE
    AND `years after registration or naturalisation` LESS THAN 5
    AND (`months of imprisonment` AT LEAST 12 OR `fine` AT LEAST 5000)
    AND (NOT `pardoned`)
    AND `continuing is not conducive to the public good`
    AND (NOT `would be stateless`)
